---
import SectionHead from "../assets/SectionHead.astro";

const services = [
  {
    n: "01",
    title: "Single-system audit",
    tag: "Start here",
    body: "You send one LLM feature and the documents it reads from. We agree what “supported” means for that system, I test it, and you get a findings list ranked by severity, with each failing claim next to the text that should have backed it.",
    note: "Small enough to approve without procurement.",
  },
  {
    n: "02",
    title: "Evaluation harness",
    body: "I build the checks into your stack: claim-level grounding, unsupported-claim rate, citation coverage, version tracing and prompt-injection tests. It is calibrated on claims your team labels by hand.",
    note: "Documented so your team runs it without me.",
  },
  {
    n: "03",
    title: "Ongoing assurance",
    body: "The same checks, re-run every month against new documents and changed systems.",
    note: "When an auditor asks, the evidence is already current.",
  },
];
---

<section id="services" class="border-b border-black/10">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-10 py-20">
    <SectionHead label="How we'd work">Start with one system.</SectionHead>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-black/70 leading-relaxed">
      Each engagement is a fixed piece of work. The audit comes first; whether a harness or
      monthly checks make sense depends on what it finds.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-px bg-black/10 border border-black/10 md:grid-cols-3">
      {services.map((s) => (
        <li class="bg-white p-7 flex flex-col">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-black/45">{s.n}</span>
            {s.tag && <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-orange">{s.tag}</span>}
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-black">{s.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-black/70 leading-relaxed">{s.body}</p>
          <p class="mt-auto pt-6 text-sm font-semibold text-black">{s.note}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-sm text-black/55 leading-relaxed">
      This is advisory work, documentation and technical testing. It is not a legal opinion, a
      conformity assessment, a certification or an attestation under any regulatory regime. I
      produce the evidence; your compliance team decides what it means.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
